-- title:
--   Weight-one adelic lift is bounded on Siegel windows
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, let $f : \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be an arbitrary function on the upper half plane, and let $C$ be a real number such that $\lVert f(\tau)\rVert \le C / \operatorname{im}(\tau)^{1/2}$ for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$; no holomorphy, invariance or other growth condition on $f$ is imposed. Form the level ideal $N = (n) \subseteq \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of $n$, and let $\varphi =$ `weightOneLift` $N\,f$ be the function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ whose value at $g$ is, when $g$ admits a decomposition $g = \gamma \cdot h \cdot u$ with $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$ embedded in the adelic points, $u$ in the compact level subgroup attached to $N$, $h$ of trivial finite component and with real archimedean image $\mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h)$ of positive determinant, the number $(f \mid_{1} \mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h))(i) \cdot \det(\mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h))$ computed from a chosen such $h$, and is $0$ when no such decomposition exists. The assertion is that $\varphi$ is bounded on Siegel windows over $\mathbb{Q}$: for all reals $c, u, d_1, d_2$ with $c > 0$ and $d_1 > 0$ and every finite set $T \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ there is a real bound $B$ with $\lVert \varphi(g) \rVert \le B$ for every $g$ lying in the union over $x \in T$ of the right translates by $x$ of the centre-cut Siegel set, that is, of the set of points whose finite component is integral, whose archimedean component has local height at least $c$ and squared $x$-window coordinate at most $u^2$ at every infinite place, and whose archimedean determinant norm lies in $[d_1, d_2]$ at every infinite place.
--
--   This is the reduction-theory growth estimate showing that the adelic lift of a classical function with the decay $\lVert f(\tau)\rVert \ll \operatorname{im}(\tau)^{-1/2}$ typical of a weight-one cusp form is bounded on finite unions of translates of centre-cut Siegel sets, the archimedean determinant being confined to a window there and the finite component integral. It is used in the construction of the adelic realisation of a primitive dihedral weight-one form, in [`DihedralWeightOne.exists_smoothCuspRealizationAt_productionPinsGeneral_toFun_eq_weightOneLift_of_isPrimitiveForm`](thm.html#DihedralWeightOne.exists_smoothCuspRealizationAt_productionPinsGeneral_toFun_eq_weightOneLift_of_isPrimitiveForm) and in [`DihedralWeightOne.weightOneLift_ne_zero_and_apply_mul_finEmbed_eq_of_isPrimitiveForm`](thm.html#DihedralWeightOne.weightOneLift_ne_zero_and_apply_mul_finEmbed_eq_of_isPrimitiveForm).
